ournament or in  this game he was at his best and decided  after 29 moves to resign some people  always ask  how would you continue in this spot well  you can see that after the night moves  doesn't matter where he moves it is  going to be a discovered check here so  it's always difficult you usually want  to get out of the way over discovered  checks so king 2 d8 maybe uh knight up  here to b7  check forking the rook here on uh d6  king e7 maybe knight takes  king takes here and then work up here to  b7 preparing for some some pretty  devastating  attacks here um you can see the queen  coming up here if you wanted to  queen up here to c7 it's a lot of  different threats that white has so  anish kiri as we said wins this game and  goes half a point behind yon for first  place  and we do have three games to go so it  is going to be  very very important that the nishkiri  has a big  game tomorrow against fabiano caruana uh  if  if he ends up losing that i do think  that it's pretty much over for him so  big day tomorrow thank you guys so much  for watching around 11 today  excited for the end of this tournament  hopefully you are as well thanks for  watching i'll see you guys  tomorrow for round 12.

